   NAME
	Load - Install or roll back a LhASsA Parts Bin package.

   FORMAT
	Load BIN=<archive.bin> [TO=<dir>] [FORCE] [QUIET] [VERBOSE] [HELP]
	Load ROLLBACK DEST=<path> [QUIET] [VERBOSE] [HELP]

   TEMPLATE
	BIN,TO/K,DEST/K,FORCE/S,ROLLBACK/S,QUIET/S,VERBOSE/S,HELP/S

   PATH
	C:Load

   FUNCTION
	Load installs a Parts Bin: an LHA archive that contains a
	Manifest, a -package.ver member, and the files to place. It
	checks OS and Requires lines, picks the best CPU/FPU/MMU/WOS/PUP
	variant for this machine, verifies destinations are writable and
	not locked, then places files with backup copies under
	SYS:T/Load. Install is two-phase (stage all candidates, then
	commit). If any step fails, Load aborts the transaction: already
	placed files are restored from bak, uncommitted T: candidates are
	discarded, and destinations are left as they were. If a restore
	cannot complete, the bak+sidecar are kept so ROLLBACK can finish
	the job. Only one Load process may run at a time.

	Absolute Manifest destinations (SDK:, LIBS:, Devs:, L:, C:,
	LOCALE:, LOCALE:Help/, SYS:Classes/, SYS:Prefs/, SYS:Tools/,
	...) are installed as written. Relative destinations go under
	InstallRoot, or under TO= when given (for example Work:Apps/MyApp/).

	After the new file is on disk, Load tries RemLibrary/RemDevice so
	the next open uses it. If the module could not be cleared, Load
	advises a reboot (exit code 5 / RETURN_WARN, including under
	QUIET). Handlers in L: and DOSDrivers always advise a reboot.
	Critical system modules are never removed mid-session.

	ROLLBACK restores a previous file from the SYS:T/Load backup
	for a given DEST path.

	Workbench: double-click a .bin (Project icon, DefaultTool Load)
	shows Load.displayme first (Next), then a confirmation requester
	(requester.class when available, otherwise EasyRequest) listing
	each destination with Manifest Ver= and whether the path already
	exists. Workbench always opens NIL: (or CON: if VERBOSE) before
	any console writes. The confirm button is Load; Cancel leaves the
	system unchanged. Errors and reboot warnings use the same path.

	Load.displayme is an Aminet readme extension written by Handle:
	Short, Author, Uploader, Type, Version, Architecture,
	Distribution, then Parts-Format / Parts-Installer / Parts-Name,
	a blank line, and install notes. LhA autoshow shows the full
	member. Load's WB requester does not dump the Key: value lines;
	it uses Parts-Name (+ Version) as the title, Short/Author as
	lead-in text, and only the prose after the blank line as the
	body (button Next). The confirm requester uses Load|Cancel.

	Only one Load may run at a time (public MsgPort LhASsA_Load).

	File: Ver= from the Manifest (written by Handle from each
	staged file's $VER:) gates upgrades by version/date. After
	extract, Load double-checks the member's $VER: matches Ver=.
	Members without Ver= are compared by size plus CRC16 of the
	first and last 256 bytes; identical copies are skipped unless
	FORCE.

   OPTIONS
	BIN=<archive.bin>
	    Path of the Bin to install (required unless ROLLBACK).

	TO=<dir>
	    Relocate relative File: destinations only. Assign paths such
	    as LIBS: and SDK: are never moved by TO=.

	DEST=<path>
	    With ROLLBACK, the installed path to restore from backup.

	FORCE
	    Allow overwrite when a file's own $VER says the candidate is
	    older or the same as the installed copy. Package (Manifest)
	    Version need not match each file. Does not force-unload
	    resident libraries or devices.

	ROLLBACK
	    Restore DEST from SYS:T/Load instead of installing a Bin.

	QUIET
	    Reduce console output. A needed reboot still returns exit
	    code 5. VERBOSE overrides QUIET for progress lines.

	VERBOSE
	    Print step-by-step progress (open Bin, Manifest, deps,
	    staging, commit). From the Shell this goes to the console.
	    From Workbench, Load opens its own CON: window. You can also
	    set a VERBOSE ToolType on Load or on the Parts Bin icon.

	HELP
	    Print this help text from HELP:<locale>/LhASsA/Load.help
	    (falls back to HELP:english/LhASsA/Load.help).

   EXAMPLES
	    1> Load BIN=ExampleLib.bin

	Installs the Bin using Manifest destinations.

	    1> Load BIN=MyApp.bin TO=Work:Apps/MyApp/

	Installs application files under Work:Apps/MyApp/.

	    1> Load BIN=ExampleLib.bin FORCE QUIET

	Forces $VER overwrite with quiet output.

	    1> Load BIN=ExampleLib.bin VERBOSE

	Installs with a step-by-step console log.

	    1> Load ROLLBACK DEST=LIBS:example.library

	Restores the previous example.library from SYS:T/Load.

   SEE ALSO
	Handle, LhX, LhA
